{"id": "EUVD-2026-103923", "enisaUuid": "0e720a1b-e8ea-3da8-ae28-327f9efc17ac", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\niio: buffer: serialize buffer teardown with mode claims\n\nBuffer-mode claims hold mlock to guarantee that the device remains in\nbuffer mode until the claim is released. Normal buffer updates take\ninfo_exist_lock followed by mlock in iio_update_buffers().\n\nHowever, iio_device_unregister() disables and deactivates all buffers\nwithout taking mlock. This can invalidate buffer state, including\nactive_scan_mask, while a buffer-mode claim is held.\n\nTake mlock in iio_disable_all_buffers() so that unregister honors the\nmode-claim lifetime guarantee. The info_exist_lock -> mlock ordering\nmatches iio_update_buffers().", "datePublished": "2026-10-18T15:45:05", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-21T12:55:33", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/6a728408ff522b749c2a3c7e68f44e861fa0dbfb", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/89f3852a28fcf7bab599280cb082baa0675536db", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/b466db9e68b4741af85f6c017e2bb0a2f025053f", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/e63188d77e10c0951bf67da6c295f768fd1abf4b", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/84bb0fc46ccf6a545b8fdf57cda83770186ed8dd"], "aliases": ["GHSA-h3hh-6rf8-4cq6", "CVE-2026-98669"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.17, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "07ea495f-d8c3-3b9a-a490-b4639c23ca66", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.18.56"}, {"id": "0d4ea56c-ce55-3e50-b57b-f96227c88410", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "5.15.137 <5.16"}, {"id": "13738bc9-8fdc-31a2-9685-b8ee7e12b607", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "6.1.60 <6.2"}, {"id": "3c3e3363-8dab-3e32-b143-d186921a8420", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "a9c471892d75847671a246619c2148578f22bbc6"}, {"id":